From 0629637aae1dc623acd9158d51b28da91c258360 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junming Chen <me@chapoly1305.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 06:31:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] [renode] Add radio_fake.cpp: null 802.15.4 radio for the
 Renode emulator

Drop-in replacement for the RAIL-backed radio.cpp, selected by the
chip_enable_fake_thread_radio GN arg. otPlatRadioTransmit records a deferred
TX success (serviced in efr32RadioProcess via otPlatRadioTxDone) and no RX is
ever delivered, so OpenThread's MLE times out and the FTD self-promotes to
Leader, forming a single-node Thread network without a functional radio.
efr32RadioInit is a no-op (never touches RAIL). Provides only the symbols
radio.cpp uniquely owned plus the sli_ot_radio_state_/events_ helpers the
still-compiled sibling files call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../platform-abstraction/efr32/radio_fake.cpp | 435 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 435 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sdk-copies/openthread/platform-abstraction/efr32/radio_fake.cpp

diff --git a/sdk-copies/openthread/platform-abstraction/efr32/radio_fake.cpp b/sdk-copies/openthread/platform-abstraction/efr32/radio_fake.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..a2c3da5e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sdk-copies/openthread/platform-abstraction/efr32/radio_fake.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,435 @@
